{"timestamp":1775018324588,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"6e2cf5bb-3f4d-4569-88d0-6d48c94f8ac2","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_0181rHysYR81Bi4iaPuuvCxM","payload":{"session_id":"6e2cf5bb-3f4d-4569-88d0-6d48c94f8ac2","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-harness-apps-mas-trees-pw-e46b0aec/6e2cf5bb-3f4d-4569-88d0-6d48c94f8ac2.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-harness/apps/mas/trees/pw-e46b0aec","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-harness/apps/mas/trees/pw-e46b0aec/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-f92767b2-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-fragment-titles.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent duplicate Fragment Title for cloned cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nAdd uniqueness validation for Fragment Title when cloning cards to prevent duplicates within the same tag path. When a duplicate is detected, automatically append a numeric suffix (-1, -2, etc.) to make the title unique.\n\n## Task Description\nCurrently, when authors clone a card in M@S Studio, it's possible to create cards with identical Fragment Title values within the same tag path. This causes confusion and data integrity issues. The solution is to implement a uniqueness check that automatically deduplicates Fragment Titles during the clone operation by appending numeric suffixes.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `studio/src/aem/aem.js` - Contains copyToFolder and createFragmentCopy methods that handle fragment duplication\n- `studio/src/aem/fragment.js` - Fragment class definition for reference\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Create Fragment Title uniqueness validation method\n- Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` method in `studio/src/aem/aem.js`\n- Method should search for existing fragments within the same tag path\n- Use the existing `searchFragment` method to query fragments by path\n- Check for title conflicts and generate unique titles with numeric suffixes\n- Follow the same pattern as existing `generateUniqueName` method\n\n### 2. Integrate uniqueness check into fragment copying\n- Modify `createFragmentCopy` method in `studio/src/aem/aem.js`\n- Before creating the fragment copy, call the new uniqueness validation method\n- Replace the original title with the unique title in the copy data\n- Ensure the logic only applies during clone/copy operations, not manual title edits\n\n### 3. Extract tag path information for scoping\n- Implement logic to determine the tag path context for uniqueness scoping\n- Extract relevant path components from the fragment path or metadata\n- Ensure uniqueness is scoped to tag path, not globally across all fragments\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Cloning a card with an existing Fragment Title generates a new unique title with a `-N` suffix\n- The suffix increments correctly if multiple clones already exist (e.g. `-1`, `-2`, `-3`)\n- Uniqueness is scoped to the tag path, not globally\n- The original card's Fragment Title is not modified\n- Manual title edits are not blocked \u2014 only auto-generated titles on clone are deduplicated\n- No two cards share the same Fragment Title + Path combination after a clone operation\n\n## Validation Commands\n- `node --check studio/src/aem/aem.js` for any changed JS files"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_0181rHysYR81Bi4iaPuuvCxM"}}
